{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nThe Projects page's only automatic refresh happens on page activation: if `LIST_REFRESH_AFTER` (5 min) has elapsed, it re-reads the linked project list (`gh repo view … projectsV2`). **The board itself (cards, Status, …) is never re-fetched except at startup and on `r`.** When the list arrives, `sync_board()` skips the fetch whenever `board_cache` already has the board.\n\nSo the data that almost never changes (repository → project links) is refreshed automatically, while the data users actually open the page for (the board) silently goes stale.\n\n## Where it hurts\n\n- Look at Projects in the morning, work on another page for a few hours, come back → the list is re-read but the board still shows the morning state; cards a teammate moved are not visible\n- Cycle several projects with `p` / `P` → each board is fetched once per session and served from cache afterwards\n- In every case there is no \"fetched N min ago\" indicator, so there is no hint that the board is stale\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Keep a fetch time per board in `board_cache`; in the `on_activate` staleness check (same 5 min threshold) and in `sync_board()` after a `Repo` result, `spawn_board()` for the selected project when its board is stale. Keep showing the old board and swap it in when the result arrives (`set_board()` already keeps the selected card by `id`, so the cursor does not jump)\n- [ ] Show the board's age in the status bar (e.g. `board 12m ago`)\n- [ ] Update `last_list_refresh` on success, so a failed fetch does not push the next retry 5 min out\n- [ ] Tests: a stale board is re-fetched on activation, a fresh one (< 5 min) is not, and a failure does not suppress the retry\n- [ ] `docs/config.md` (add a note on refresh timing if the page's section describes it)\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Periodic refresh while the page is shown (`on_tick`) — to be decided together with the `github-poll-interval` design in #135 (boards want minutes, not the runs' 5 s)\n\n## Cost\n\n`fetch_board` is `field-list` + `item-list` (up to 500 items), roughly 2–7 requests. Once per 5 min on page activation is negligible next to the GitHub page's 5 s workflow-run polling.\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T06:36:28Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":140,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Projects: re-fetch the board on page activation and show its age"}
